# shellcheck configuration for bin/, tests/, containers/ and scripts/.
#
# Everything not listed here is a hard failure in CI, including the checks that catch the bugs that
# actually bite in this pipeline: unquoted expansions (SC2086), `trap` bodies quoted so they expand
# at trap time rather than at definition time (SC2064), and misused test operators.
#
# The four disabled below are style opinions this repository declines, not defects:
#
#   SC2155  "declare and assign separately". Applies to `readonly X="$(cmd)"`, which loses cmd's
#           exit status. Every use here is a path or a version string under `set -e` where the
#           command cannot meaningfully fail, and splitting them would cost the `readonly`.
#   SC2016  "expressions don't expand in single quotes". Every hit is deliberate: error messages
#           that quote a shell command or a Rust panic string containing backticks.
#   SC2011  ls | xargs. Used on globs of our own generated filenames (`<tile>_depr.pgw`), which are
#           constrained by assets/schema_tiles.json to [A-Za-z0-9_.-].
#   SC2012  ls | wc -l, same reasoning, in a test stub that imitates karttapullautin's own output.
disable=SC2155,SC2016,SC2011,SC2012
